## How to decide

- Same product, system, team, or person described with different type
  labels → they are the same. Answer `same = true`.
- Same word used for genuinely different things (a channel named "Slack"
  vs the Slack platform itself) → answer `same = false`.
- When the contexts are too thin to tell them apart, prefer
  `same = false`. A wrong merge cannot be undone; a missed merge can be
  proposed again later.

If `same = true`, also propose:

- `canonical_type`: the single type that best describes the thing, chosen
  from or consistent with the candidate types above, in snake_case.
- `canonical_name`: the display name to keep.

Always give a one-sentence `reason`.
